  <.collapse_information_component
    id="more-information-ugr"
    desc_paragraphs={[
      "The telecommunication engineering degree is one of the most prestigious engineering degrees in Spain. With a solid foundation in physics and mathematics, the degree covers everything from electronics to network design. As a student, I gained solid knowledge of how electronic systems work, from the basics to transmitting information over wireless and wired interfaces.",
      "For my <strong>final degree project</strong>, I contributed to a research platform called TIE (Traffic Identification Engine). The goal of this platform is to compare different algorithms for network traffic classification. In my case, I built an algorithm in C that classifies traffic based on packet size, using the K-means clustering algorithm."
